hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24250","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Muslim ibn Sallam, from Isa ibn Hittan, from Ali ibn Talq, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you passes wind, let him perform ablution, and do not come to women in their posteriors, for Allah is not shy of the truth."
"24251","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Isa ibn Hittan, from Muslim ibn Sallam, from Ali ibn Talq, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in desert land, and one of us has a light wind, and water is scarce. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes wind, let him perform ablution, and do not come to women in their backsides, for Allah is not shy of the truth."
"24252","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, I heard Isa ibn Hittan narrating from Muslim ibn Sallam, and he mentioned the hadith."
"24253","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim, from Isa ibn Hittan, from Muslim ibn Sallam, from Ali ibn Talq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that women be approached in their backsides, for Allah is not shy of the truth."
